1
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:11,159
Boss.

2
00:01:12,599 --> 00:01:13,640
Give me a stick of RAM.

3
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:15,560
Just one?

4
00:01:16,079 --> 00:01:17,359
Think you're buying a sausage?

5
00:01:17,640 --> 00:01:18,359
I don't sell just one.

6
00:01:18,359 --> 00:01:19,239
Wholesale only, ten minimum.

7
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:25,200
You want 'em or not?

8
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:41,640
Police.

9
00:01:42,239 --> 00:01:43,040
Let's talk.

10
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:47,920
Sure. What about?

11
00:01:47,959 --> 00:01:49,480
About the RAM sticks.

12
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:49,959
Okay.

13
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:50,840
Or let's talk about...

14
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:53,640
...how out at sea,

15
00:01:53,640 --> 00:01:55,760
...you were forced to jump at gunpoint.

16
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:56,560
Either works.

17
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:00,719
Who are you?

18
00:02:03,599 --> 00:02:04,400
Digging into me?

19
00:02:05,439 --> 00:02:06,640
Take a look at this.

20
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:11,360
See if you placed this order.

21
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:12,199
Let's see...

22
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:15,639
I really don't remember.

23
00:02:16,319 --> 00:02:17,680
I place way too many orders.

24
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:18,240
Understood.

25
00:02:18,439 --> 00:02:19,520
Figured you wouldn't.

26
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:20,400
No problem.

27
00:02:20,599 --> 00:02:21,439
Tell you what.

28
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:23,759
Let's go somewhere else.

29
00:02:23,759 --> 00:02:25,520
Maybe a new place will jog your memory.

30
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:26,199
Think about...

31
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:28,639
...what's in this shop...

32
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:30,840
...that might be smuggled.

33
00:02:32,159 --> 00:02:34,520
Think about those overseas burner accounts.

34
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:35,719
Let me take a look, man.

35
00:02:35,919 --> 00:02:36,280
Let me check.

36
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:37,000
Ringing any bells?

37
00:02:37,039 --> 00:02:37,680
Just looking.

38
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:38,280
Let me just see.

39
00:02:38,719 --> 00:02:39,280
I remember.

40
00:02:39,919 --> 00:02:40,919
I do remember.

41
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:42,560
I remember the name. A woman.

42
00:02:42,919 --> 00:02:44,120
A woman bought that.

43
00:02:44,639 --> 00:02:45,560
Take your time. No rush.

44
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:46,759
Pepper spray. Self-defense spray.

45
00:02:46,759 --> 00:02:47,719
She worked the night shift, I think.

46
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:49,439
Let me check her messages first.

47
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:50,520
Right, right.

48
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:52,719
A woman in her 30s bought pepper spray.

49
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:57,039
Selling that isn't illegal, right?

50
00:02:57,199 --> 00:02:59,159
I was just helping out, right?

51
00:02:59,159 --> 00:03:00,439
Save it.

52
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:02,240
Let me see the delivery address.

53
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:05,439
Got it, got it. Right here.

54
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:08,080
Address and phone number are both here.

55
00:03:09,199 --> 00:03:10,680
38 Taichun Street.

56
00:03:13,199 --> 00:03:14,199
Right, number 38.

57
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:17,199
See how easy that was?

58
00:03:18,159 --> 00:03:18,960
Thanks.

59
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:20,159
Don't mention it.

60
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:22,120
Hold on, man...

61
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:26,800
Who told you about jumping into the sea?

62
00:03:34,199 --> 00:03:35,039
Let me tell you.

63
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:37,000
If you don't want people to know...

64
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:37,879
...don't do it in the first place.

65
00:03:37,879 --> 00:03:38,120
Right.

66
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:38,560
The net of justice is wide...

67
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:39,240
...and lets nothing through.

68
00:03:39,719 --> 00:03:40,840
As for Xu Xiaoguan's case...

69
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:42,439
...learn your lesson.

70
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:45,479
Thank you.

71
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:50,280
Are you sure this is the place?

72
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:53,159
Positive.

73
00:03:54,719 --> 00:03:56,360
The delivery was a week before the crime.

74
00:03:57,319 --> 00:03:59,120
The timeline matches up perfectly.

75
00:04:07,719 --> 00:04:09,039
I know this guy.

76
00:04:10,639 --> 00:04:11,479
His name is Liu Qiang.

77
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:14,639
He's a friend of Hou Ru's brother.

78
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:18,040
I investigated him for the missing family.

79
00:04:19,279 --> 00:04:21,439
Too bad we didn't find any evidence then.

80
00:04:22,399 --> 00:04:23,079
Tail him.

81
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:26,279
Take it easy.

82
00:05:05,399 --> 00:05:06,560
That's Hou Ru's car.

83
00:05:15,199 --> 00:05:16,079
Next clip.

84
00:05:25,279 --> 00:05:26,639
She followed her for two kilometers.

85
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:28,759
Once she saw her enter the compound,

86
00:05:29,160 --> 00:05:30,199
she finally turned around and left.

87
00:05:35,879 --> 00:05:36,680
Stop.

88
00:05:40,199 --> 00:05:41,000
This woman

89
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:42,839
definitely isn't working alone.

90
00:05:43,079 --> 00:05:44,680
There must be someone else.

91
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:29,079
Mentor, Mentor!

92
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:31,319
Woman in red spotted.

93
00:06:31,319 --> 00:06:32,560
Target acquired.

94
00:06:33,879 --> 00:06:35,240
Copy that. Move in.

95
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:38,920
Copy.

96
00:06:47,399 --> 00:06:47,720
Freeze!

97
00:06:47,879 --> 00:06:48,439
Don't move! Don't move!

98
00:06:48,439 --> 00:06:49,319
Nobody move!

99
00:07:03,879 --> 00:07:04,680
Hou Dong.

100
00:07:10,959 --> 00:07:11,639
Zhang Weihong.

101
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:13,639
34 years old.

102
00:07:14,319 --> 00:07:16,439
Husband: Li Zhiqiang, 36 years old.

103
00:07:16,759 --> 00:07:17,959
Roast goose shop owner.

104
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,399
Son: Li Ming, 13 years old.

105
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:21,439
7th grader at County No. 2 Middle School.

106
00:07:22,279 --> 00:07:23,120
Boarding student.

107
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:25,680
Third in his class in monthly math exams.

108
00:07:25,680 --> 00:07:26,560
Good student.

109
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:28,279
Is that all accurate?

110
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:30,879
Does your son still think

111
00:07:30,879 --> 00:07:32,800
you're working nights at the factory?

112
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,560
He doesn't know what you did, does he?

113
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:39,920
Zhang Weihong.

114
00:07:40,879 --> 00:07:41,839
You're a mother.

115
00:07:41,839 --> 00:07:43,040
You're a wife.

116
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:44,759
And now, a murderer.

117
00:07:45,959 --> 00:07:46,600
Tell us.

118
00:07:46,959 --> 00:07:47,920
Why did you kill?

119
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:49,319
Speak.

120
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:53,480
How did you meet Hou Dong?

121
00:07:55,759 --> 00:07:57,000
Online.

122
00:07:58,040 --> 00:07:58,759
Online?

123
00:07:59,079 --> 00:07:59,839
Where online?

124
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:04,199
A philosophy forum.

125
00:08:04,519 --> 00:08:05,680
How did you two start talking?

126
00:08:06,759 --> 00:08:08,160
When business was slow,

127
00:08:08,439 --> 00:08:10,240
I'd play on my phone in the back.

128
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:15,360
I came across a forum.

129
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:18,319
The posts on there made a lot of sense.

130
00:08:20,879 --> 00:08:22,480
One day, I left a comment,

131
00:08:24,279 --> 00:08:25,720
and he replied to me.

132
00:08:26,279 --> 00:08:27,079
What did he say?

133
00:08:29,879 --> 00:08:33,159
He said, "You're a very good person."

134
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:40,039
And you believed what he said

135
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:40,960
was true right then?

136
00:08:50,320 --> 00:08:52,000
Ever since my parents passed away,

137
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:53,720
no one had spoken to me like that.

138
00:08:54,919 --> 00:08:56,440
Nobody cared about me.

139
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:05,679
Then we started chatting online.

140
00:09:07,279 --> 00:09:08,360
He also talked to me about

141
00:09:08,360 --> 00:09:11,039
the Bible, the I Ching, The Art of War...

142
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:12,440
He knew everything.

143
00:09:13,039 --> 00:09:14,399
And you believed what he said?

144
00:09:14,759 --> 00:09:16,720
Ever since my son started middle school,

145
00:09:19,279 --> 00:09:20,399
he boarded at school.

146
00:09:20,639 --> 00:09:22,200
On weekends, he'd lock himself

147
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:23,440
in his room playing games,

148
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:24,200
completely ignoring me.

149
00:09:24,200 --> 00:09:25,120
He found me annoying.

150
00:09:28,159 --> 00:09:29,360
My husband was even worse.

151
00:09:30,519 --> 00:09:32,000
To him, I didn't even exist.

152
00:09:33,279 --> 00:09:35,559
But Brother Dong messaged me every day.

153
00:09:35,559 --> 00:09:36,759
Good morning, good night.

154
00:09:38,799 --> 00:09:40,320
We really connected.

155
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:44,679
When did you meet?

156
00:09:48,799 --> 00:09:49,759
Six months ago.

157
00:09:53,159 --> 00:09:54,480
How did you feel when you saw him?

158
00:10:00,039 --> 00:10:02,720
I only learned of his bad leg when we met.

159
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:08,879
His...

160
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:11,399
life was miserable, too.

161
00:10:13,919 --> 00:10:16,759
We were both abandoned by the world.

162
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:19,039
What did you think of his bad leg?

163
00:10:19,399 --> 00:10:20,120
I accepted it.

164
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:21,000
It didn't matter.

165
00:10:21,559 --> 00:10:22,440
Why didn't it matter?

166
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:28,200
Because he was my savior.

167
00:10:33,559 --> 00:10:34,639
Where is Hou Dong?

168
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:40,159
Can I see him?

169
00:10:49,480 --> 00:10:50,399
Was he the one

170
00:10:51,639 --> 00:10:52,960
who had you

171
00:10:53,879 --> 00:10:55,200
kill his sister?

172
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:14,639
I did that of my own free will.

173
00:11:22,399 --> 00:11:24,039
Her husband sells roast goose.

174
00:11:24,440 --> 00:11:25,480
She's the one slaughtering the geese.

175
00:11:26,399 --> 00:11:27,720
She kills over a hundred a day.

176
00:11:30,559 --> 00:11:31,799
No wonder she's so ruthless.

177
00:11:34,639 --> 00:11:35,600
The key is Hou Dong.

178
00:11:37,519 --> 00:11:39,519
Let's check out his secret hideout.

179
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:48,039
This is it.

180
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:50,000
Get out of the car.

181
00:11:58,679 --> 00:12:00,480
That's it. See the tree right here?

182
00:12:09,039 --> 00:12:09,960
Not this one.

183
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:16,399
He sure picked a place...

184
00:12:17,039 --> 00:12:17,840
pretty secretive.

185
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:19,799
This one.

186
00:12:20,120 --> 00:12:20,799
See it?

187
00:12:20,799 --> 00:12:21,399
Number six.

188
00:12:56,039 --> 00:12:56,799
Not here.

189
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:58,720
It's not over here.

190
00:13:00,600 --> 00:13:01,480
Look at this place.

191
00:13:03,480 --> 00:13:04,840
All hidden in the nooks and crannies.

192
00:13:05,840 --> 00:13:06,559
Seriously.

193
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:09,320
Most people would never find him here.

194
00:13:09,320 --> 00:13:10,159
Nobody'd ever think to look here.

195
00:13:15,519 --> 00:13:16,320
There's a staircase here.

196
00:13:17,159 --> 00:13:18,399
It probably leads upstairs.

197
00:13:28,399 --> 00:13:29,080
Go up here.

198
00:13:31,440 --> 00:13:32,200
Careful.

199
00:13:37,080 --> 00:13:37,919
It's right here.

200
00:13:39,039 --> 00:13:40,120
That's it.

201
00:13:41,519 --> 00:13:42,440
Take it easy.

202
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:46,799
Come on, take a look.

203
00:13:47,799 --> 00:13:48,480
Check it out.

204
00:14:05,799 --> 00:14:07,440
A temporary hideout,

205
00:14:11,039 --> 00:14:12,600
yet so neatly organized.

206
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:15,320
This guy...

207
00:14:16,399 --> 00:14:17,120
is something else.

208
00:14:25,480 --> 00:14:26,919
That's not just organized.

209
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:29,600
He's conducting experiments here.

210
00:14:32,399 --> 00:14:33,039
Tell me.

211
00:14:33,519 --> 00:14:34,519
What do you think?

212
00:14:39,039 --> 00:14:41,840
He might be physically disabled,

213
00:14:41,879 --> 00:14:44,120
but his mind is sharper than anyone's.

214
00:14:45,120 --> 00:14:46,080
And your thoughts?

215
00:14:53,440 --> 00:14:55,440
He's no accomplice to Zhang Weihong.

216
00:14:58,039 --> 00:14:59,919
He orchestrated the whole thing.

217
00:15:04,519 --> 00:15:06,440
Your parents have been missing six months,

218
00:15:07,039 --> 00:15:08,440
and so have you.

219
00:15:09,399 --> 00:15:10,679
Do you really think

220
00:15:11,919 --> 00:15:13,440
this explanation holds up?

221
00:15:15,759 --> 00:15:16,919
My depression flared up,

222
00:15:17,080 --> 00:15:18,519
so I retreated to a temple to recover.

223
00:15:18,600 --> 00:15:19,720
My phone was turned off.

224
00:15:19,799 --> 00:15:20,840
You went on a retreat,

225
00:15:22,120 --> 00:15:23,679
and your parents vanished?

226
00:15:23,679 --> 00:15:25,279
Just a twist of fate.

227
00:15:25,279 --> 00:15:26,480
I'm a victim too.

228
00:15:27,200 --> 00:15:28,759
You're great at spinning lies,

229
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:32,200
but none of them sound human.

230
00:15:33,399 --> 00:15:34,440
Maybe that's because

231
00:15:34,919 --> 00:15:36,120
I have a clear conscience.

232
00:15:43,919 --> 00:15:45,080
How about

233
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:46,519
I tell your story instead?

234
00:15:49,519 --> 00:15:50,559
First, we know

235
00:15:51,039 --> 00:15:52,200
you killed your parents.

236
00:15:53,399 --> 00:15:54,200
You were talented,

237
00:15:54,679 --> 00:15:55,559
top of your class.

238
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:56,919
Yet because of your disability,

239
00:15:57,360 --> 00:15:58,159
your classmates bullied you relentlessly.

240
00:15:58,159 --> 00:15:59,000
Come on, take it! Grab it!

241
00:15:59,039 --> 00:16:00,000
Not giving it to you!

242
00:16:00,240 --> 00:16:01,480
College? What college?

243
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,519
A cripple like you wants to go to college?

244
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:06,320
I'm telling you one last time:

245
00:16:06,639 --> 00:16:08,639
stay put and learn medicine from me.

246
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:10,799
Dad, I really want to study.

247
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:13,480
You wanted to prove yourself in the exams,

248
00:16:14,039 --> 00:16:15,600
but your father forced you to give up.

249
00:16:16,159 --> 00:16:17,120
He was a doctor,

250
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:18,559
yet he couldn't cure you.

251
00:16:19,720 --> 00:16:21,279
You saw that as a disgrace,

252
00:16:21,759 --> 00:16:23,200
and even worse, a betrayal.

253
00:16:24,679 --> 00:16:25,840
You devoured countless books.

254
00:16:26,120 --> 00:16:27,159
Even with an ancient classic

255
00:16:27,159 --> 00:16:28,600
as obscure as the I Ching,

256
00:16:28,759 --> 00:16:30,000
you could recite it from memory.

257
00:16:31,080 --> 00:16:32,200
You saw yourself as a hidden dragon,

258
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:34,399
bound to soar high one day.

259
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:36,559
The internet gave you wings.

260
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:39,120
You preached and gave advice on forums,

261
00:16:39,279 --> 00:16:41,039
becoming a revered moderator.

262
00:16:41,559 --> 00:16:44,279
Your philosophy captivated a housewife:

263
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:45,919
Zhang Weihong.

264
00:16:47,519 --> 00:16:48,639
I want to meet you.

265
00:16:49,200 --> 00:16:50,399
Not out of curiosity,

266
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:52,840
but because you make my heart race.

267
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:04,880
I love your mind,

268
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:06,039
not your body.

269
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,240
You finally showed up.

270
00:17:21,799 --> 00:17:22,720
In her eyes,

271
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:24,480
you aren't disabled,

272
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:25,559
but Sun Bin,

273
00:17:25,839 --> 00:17:26,759
Shi Tiesheng,

274
00:17:29,319 --> 00:17:31,480
a genius overlooked by the world.

275
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:38,559
But even geniuses must obey the law.

276
00:17:40,799 --> 00:17:42,559
You wanted a divorce long ago, didn't you?

277
00:17:43,960 --> 00:17:45,079
That mute wife of yours,

278
00:17:45,079 --> 00:17:46,319
arranged by your parents,

279
00:17:46,880 --> 00:17:47,880
lived with you for years,

280
00:17:48,200 --> 00:17:49,680
yet you never showed her any warmth.

281
00:17:51,279 --> 00:17:52,839
You only wanted to be with Zhang Weihong.

282
00:17:52,839 --> 00:17:54,119
You thought she understood you,

283
00:17:54,119 --> 00:17:56,440
adored you, ready to leave her family.

284
00:17:57,880 --> 00:17:58,640
You wanted her,

285
00:17:59,559 --> 00:18:00,799
and you wanted freedom.

286
00:18:04,680 --> 00:18:06,200
But your dad was no pushover.

287
00:18:06,799 --> 00:18:07,680
He even mocked you, saying,

288
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:10,759
"A cripple like you thinks he can be picky?"

289
00:18:13,200 --> 00:18:14,319
Over a decade of resentment

290
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:16,480
exploded at that very moment.

291
00:18:19,039 --> 00:18:20,440
When you struck,

292
00:18:20,680 --> 00:18:22,160
she was right beside you, wasn't she?

293
00:18:25,039 --> 00:18:26,559
Your dad had just finished a cigarette,

294
00:18:27,039 --> 00:18:28,640
sitting on the couch, cursing you out.

295
00:18:30,279 --> 00:18:32,480
You took a hammer to the back of his head.

296
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:35,039
He didn't even get a chance to fight back.

297
00:18:35,119 --> 00:18:36,400
Your mom tried to run, too,

298
00:18:36,799 --> 00:18:39,680
but you hammered her down again and again,

299
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:41,559
until her fingernails broke.
